  "description": "UVETEV crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C154 H167 Gd7 N2 O36 2+,2(N1 O3 1-). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 1.611-3.884 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 35.89-119.65°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd7(OH)6(thmeH2)5(thmeH)(tpa)6(MeCN)2](NO3)2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
